35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"- **Kenji**: @Mizuki @Asuka @Rin @Servas I found the yard scanners are a mess of old models, and the 2021 trial failed fast.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Asuka"",""Rin"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"- **Mizuki**: @Kenji That explains the friction. My invoices show separately licensed pieces climbing yearly, while bundled deals held steady.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Mizuki That confirms my fear. Support was unowned for two days last winter, and our frozen scope broke within a year.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,- **Rin**: @Asuka That sounds scary! I found the 2018 pay move had mismatched codes for a whole year. We need to avoid that mess.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: @Rin A year of errors is a long time to suffer. I found two key administrators retire this year, and the last hiring took eleven months.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"- **Kenji**: @Servas That staffing gap is terrifying. My depot calendar shows no freeze window in winter, so a bad cutover means total chaos.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,- **Mizuki**: @Kenji That winter chaos is exactly why I’m watching the recurring costs. We can’t afford a failed cutover that triggers emergency spending.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Mizuki Agreed. The unowned support and shifting scope mean we need a vendor who stays accountable, not just a cheap license.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"- **Rin**: @Asuka Exactly! If the data is messy, the whole thing falls apart. We need someone who fixes the mess, not just adds to it.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,- **Servas**: @Rin The data is only half the story. I found supervisors quietly dropped the new steps within weeks. We must respect their routines.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"- **Kenji**: @Servas That’s a real risk. If the yard crew ignores the new system, we’re back to paper. We need something they’ll actually use.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"- **Mizuki**: @Kenji Precisely. If the yard rejects it, we pay for a system we can’t use. That’s the hidden cost I’m tracking.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
